      "worked_solution": "Remember that $csc$ is the reciprocal of $sin.$ So\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡C=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡C}.\n$$\n\nWe have that $m∠C={45}^{∘},$ which is a special angle, and its sine has the value\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡C=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡C & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡C} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
